$\begin{align}
f'(x)&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[ x\sqrt{4-x} \right]
\\\\
&=x\cdot \dfrac{d}{dx}[\sqrt{4-x}]+ \dfrac{d}{dx}[x] \cdot \sqrt{4-x}
\\\\
&=x\cdot \dfrac{1}{2\sqrt{4-x}}\cdot \dfrac{d}{dx}[4-x]+1\cdot \sqrt{4-x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-x}{2\sqrt{4-x}}+\sqrt{4-x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{8-3x}{2\sqrt{4-x}}
\end{align}$

Now let's look for $x$-values where $f'$ is zero or undefined.
